speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, I think the comments of my hon. collegue make a good deal of sense. Our point was not as to substance but as to form. Standing Order 99(2) states;
Within 120 days of the presentation of a report from a standing or special committee, the government shall, upon the request of the committee, table a comprehensive response thereto.
We are simply seeking direction so we know exactly what we are being asked to respond to in the future. As my colleague states, this the first time we have had this particular situation arise and I think we would all like to set a good precedent which could be followed with ease by all Members of the House in the future.
